          "end": 17.83,
          "en": "of the Composition API module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.83,
          "end": 19.64,
          "en": "and at the end of that module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.64,
          "end": 23.52,
          "en": "we migrated that project from the Options API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.52,
          "end": 25.173,
          "en": "to the Composition API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.37,
          "end": 30.7,
          "en": "Now you find that latest snapshot attached to this lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.7,
          "end": 33.67,
          "en": "because I wanna pick up on that, I wanna start there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.67,
          "end": 37.23,
          "en": "and now talk about reusing functionality",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.23,
          "end": 40.57,
          "en": "because that's something we haven't done in that project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.57,
          "end": 41.9,
          "en": "up to that point.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.9,
          "end": 46.41,
          "en": "We stopped when we migrated it to the Composition API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.41,
          "end": 50.41,
          "en": "but now I wanna reuse some functionality.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.41,
          "end": 53.11,
          "en": "And there is one main functionality",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.11,
          "end": 55.06,
          "en": "which I would like to reuse.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.06,
          "end": 59.78,
          "en": "In UserList.vue, I got my search functionality,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.78,
          "end": 62.95,
          "en": "two pieces of data, a computed property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.95,
          "end": 66.15,
          "en": "and a watcher and this function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.15,
          "end": 70.41,
          "en": "And we have pretty much the same in ProjectsList",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.41,
          "end": 73.03999999999999,
          "en": "we're dealing with different data there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.03999999999999,
          "end": 75.96000000000001,
          "en": "here we have a list of projects which we filter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.96000000000001,
          "end": 79.99,
          "en": "in UserList we have a list of users, but besides that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.99,
          "end": 81.793,
          "en": "it's the same functionality.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.76,
          "end": 85.76,
          "en": "So let's see how we can now use a custom hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.76,
          "end": 88.31,
          "en": "to outsource this into a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.31,
          "end": 92.003,
          "en": "which we can then use in both UserList and ProjectsList.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.07,
          "end": 96.63,
          "en": "For this, I'll add a new folder next two components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.63,
          "end": 98.4,
          "en": "and I will again, name it hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.4,
          "end": 101.94,
          "en": "And in there I will add a search.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.94,
          "end": 105.07,
          "en": "There I'll add a function, useSearch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.07,
          "end": 108.4,
          "en": "following that naming pattern which I recommended,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.4,
          "end": 112.12,
          "en": "and I will already export it because I plan on using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.12,
          "end": 114.113,
          "en": "and calling useSearch in UserList and ProjectsList.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.03999999999999,
          "end": 118.96000000000001,
          "en": "Now, as I mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.96000000000001,
          "end": 122.24,
          "en": "there is a lot of functionality we have in common.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.24,
          "end": 125.08,
          "en": "So why don't we just go to UserList",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.08,
          "end": 128.72,
          "en": "and maybe grab all that code here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.72,
          "end": 133.56,
          "en": "So the two refs, the computed property, availableUsers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.56,
          "end": 136.69,
          "en": "the watcher, and this updateSearch function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.61,
          "end": 140.53,
          "en": "and copy it into search.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.53,
          "end": 144.103,
          "en": "into our useSearch function like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 147.02,
          "end": 148.7,
          "en": "Now we need to add a import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 149.59,
          "end": 151.85,
          "en": "because I'm using a bunch of features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 151.85,
          "end": 154.4,
          "en": "which are not available in that file yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 154.4,
          "end": 157.38,
          "en": "The ref functions, the computed function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 157.38,
          "end": 160.8,
          "en": "the watch function, yeah, that should be it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 160.8,
          "end": 162.88,
          "en": "So we should add an import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 162.88,
          "end": 165.46,
          "en": "and import from the view framework,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165.46,
          "end": 166.67000000000002,
          "en": "And there specifically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 166.67000000000002,
          "end": 169.63,
          "en": "I wanna import ref, computed and watch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 169.63,
          "end": 171.45,
          "en": "since these are the three functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 171.45,
          "end": 173.223,
          "en": "I'm using in this file now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 174.32999999999998,
          "end": 177.8,
          "en": "With that, that code showed almost work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 177.8,
          "end": 179.72,
          "en": "not entirely though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 179.72,
          "end": 182.2,
          "en": "One problem which we will face",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 182.2,
          "end": 185.86,
          "en": "is that we depend on props.users filter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 185.86,
          "end": 188.95,
          "en": "Now in this function, props is not available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 188.95,
          "end": 192.16,
          "en": "Even if we call it in our setup method later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 192.16,
          "end": 195.763,
          "en": "inside of the scope of dysfunction props doesn't exist.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 197.02,
          "end": 198.93,
          "en": "But of course we can work around that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 198.93,
          "end": 202.65,
          "en": "We can simply add a parameter and maybe name it items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 202.65,
          "end": 206.3,
          "en": "to have a generic function that works on any kind of items,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.3,
          "end": 209.4,
          "en": "no matter if that's people or projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 209.4,
          "end": 212.3,
          "en": "That's why I'm just naming it items to make it clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 212.3,
          "end": 215.05,
          "en": "that this should work on any kind of array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 215.05,
          "end": 220.05,
          "en": "And then we could use items.filter here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 220.3,
          "end": 224.54,
          "en": "and also replace props.users with items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 224.54,
          "end": 227.423,
          "en": "in the other places here like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 228.61,
          "end": 231.99,
          "en": "And I'll rename my user's helper variable here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 231.99,
          "end": 236.53,
          "en": "to filteredItems and use that in all the places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 239.18,
          "end": 242.563,
          "en": "where I used users to make this more generic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 243.58,
          "end": 246.5,
          "en": "I will also rename the entire computer property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 246.5,
          "end": 247.5,
          "en": "to a availableItems,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 248.52,
          "end": 251.12,
          "en": "because this is now no longer focused on users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 251.12,
          "end": 253.483,
          "en": "but on any items we wanna search.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 254.86,
          "end": 256.82,
          "en": "Now, we will still have a problem though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 256.82,
          "end": 259.86,
          "en": "The function which has passed to filter here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 259.86,
          "end": 263.07,
          "en": "has specific logic for filtering",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 263.07,
          "end": 266.15,
          "en": "that will only work on our users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 266.15,
          "end": 268.573,
          "en": "because here I'm filtering on a full name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 269.43,
          "end": 272.983,
          "en": "In ProjectsList, for example, I'm filtering on a title.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 273.82,
          "end": 276.90999999999997,
          "en": "Now there are two ways of making this work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 276.90999999999997,
          "end": 280.01,
          "en": "We could accept this filtering function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 280.01,
          "end": 283.90999999999997,
          "en": "as a number parameter, a filter function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 283.90999999999997,
          "end": 288.90999999999997,
          "en": "which we then, for example, just pass here like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 290.72,
          "end": 292.58,
          "en": "that would be one alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 292.58,
          "end": 294.75,
          "en": "Then we have to pass in the function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 294.75,
          "end": 297.02,
          "en": "that should be used here from the place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 297.02,
          "end": 299.32,
          "en": "where we call useSearch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 299.32,
          "end": 304.32,
          "en": "Or if we know that we will always operate on an item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 304.59,
          "end": 307.72,
          "en": "but the property which holds the text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 307.72,
          "end": 309.2,
          "en": "we wanna use for filtering",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 309.2,
          "end": 311.54,
          "en": "has a different name all the time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 311.54,
          "end": 314.43,
          "en": "then we could also just accept a second argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 314.43,
          "end": 317.35,
          "en": "which stores that specific property name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 317.35,
          "end": 322.35,
          "en": "off the values we're trying to search in a given component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 322.48,
          "end": 324.18,
          "en": "So then for example here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 324.18,
          "end": 327.63,
          "en": "we could add a search prop or whatever you want to name it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 327.63,
          "end": 332.303,
          "en": "parameter, and simply access userSearchProp.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 334.87,
          "end": 338.6,
          "en": "So dynamically access a property based on the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 338.6,
          "end": 340.08299999999997,
          "en": "we get on this parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 340.95,
          "end": 345.26,
          "en": "And maybe rename this from user to item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 345.26,
          "end": 346.93,
          "en": "So both works, but with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 346.93,
          "end": 349.933,
          "en": "we have a more flexible filtering logic here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 351.96,
          "end": 354.27,
          "en": "Now we also have a watcher here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 354.27,
          "end": 356.759,
          "en": "where we watch the enteredSearchTerm.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 356.759,
          "end": 357.88,
          "en": "And whenever that search term changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 360.082,
          "end": 363.54,
          "en": "we trigger this function and set this timer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 363.54,
          "end": 366.63,
          "en": "Now, here we can leave everything the way it is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 366.63,
          "end": 370.23,
          "en": "because both enteredSearchTerm and activeSearchTerm",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 370.23,
          "end": 372.6,
          "en": "are refs defined in this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 372.6,
          "end": 374.373,
          "en": "and therefore will be available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 375.52,
          "end": 378.64,
          "en": "And updateSearch should also work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 378.64,
          "end": 379.473,
          "en": "So with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 379.473,
          "end": 380.74,
          "en": "the only thing we gotta do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 380.74,
          "end": 383.29,
          "en": "is we have to return a bunch of things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 383.29,
          "end": 384.53,
          "en": "so that we can use them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 384.53,
          "end": 386.38,
          "en": "in the components set up method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 386.38,
          "end": 388.87,
          "en": "where we're going to call, useSearch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 390.03,
          "end": 391.87,
          "en": "And as I mentioned, it's your function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 391.87,
          "end": 394.92,
          "en": "So it's up to you, how you return these things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 394.92,
          "end": 398.35,
          "en": "if you bundle them together in an array or in an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 398.35,
          "end": 400.63,
          "en": "And here I'll go for an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 400.63,
          "end": 403.493,
          "en": "Before we saw an array, both is possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 404.43,
          "end": 406.01,
          "en": "Here I'll go for an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 406.01,
          "end": 409.61,
          "en": "And now let's think about what we wanna expose",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 409.61,
          "end": 412.153,
          "en": "to the component that calls useSearch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 413.77,
          "end": 415.97,
          "en": "For that let's maybe go back to UserList",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 415.97,
          "end": 417.65999999999997,
          "en": "because that will be a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 417.65999999999997,
          "end": 419.86,
          "en": "which will soon use this custom hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
